# WealthHabit frontend — PRODUCTION build environment (example only).
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the JavaScript bundle at BUILD time.
# Consequences:
#   * the value is baked into the image — changing it means rebuilding;
#   * it ships to the browser, so devtools exposes it to every visitor;
#   * NEVER put a secret, token or password here.
#
# Building with Docker passes the value as a build argument instead of a file:
#   docker build -f client/Dockerfile --build-arg VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/api .
# Copy this file to client/.env.production (git-ignored) only when you build
# the client outside Docker; Vite loads it automatically in production mode.

# API base URL used by the browser.
#
# Default (leave unset or empty): the bundle calls the same origin at "/api",
# and the client image proxies /api to the API container (API_PROXY_PASS).
# This is the supported deployment: same origin, no CORS, refresh cookie stays
# SameSite=Lax.
#
# Set an absolute URL (https://api.example.com/api) ONLY when the frontend and
# the API are served from different origins. Then also set, on the server:
#   CLIENT_URL         = this frontend origin (CORS)
#   COOKIE_SAME_SITE   = none, COOKIE_SECURE = true (cross-site refresh cookie)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
